// 1. L-SHADE init: H=5, M_F[]=M_CR[]=0.5, N_min = max(4, dim), archive A, p in [2/N, 0.2]
// 2. for each i: sample $F\sim\mathrm{Cauchy}(M_F[r],0.1)$, $CR\sim\mathcal{N}(M_{CR}[r],0.1)$
// 3.   strategy $\sim$ Uniform({rand, pbest, best})
// 4.     rand: $v = x_{r1} + F(x_{r2}-x_{r3})$
// 5.     pbest: $v = x_i + F(x_{\text{pbest}}-x_i) + F(x_{r1}-x_{r2 (\cup A)})$
// 6.     best: $v = x_{\text{best}} + F(x_{r1}-x_{r2})$
// 7. binomial CR; greedy select; success-history Lehmer/arith updates
// 8. linear pop reduction every gen; if no improvement for 100 gens, restart pop around best

